00:58:40.360 --> 00:58:42.410
and who should be next in line?

00:58:42.410 --> 00:58:44.020
You could make it a cabinet officer,

00:58:44.020 --> 00:58:45.410
again handpicked by the President,

00:58:45.410 --> 00:58:48.380
Secretary of State,
defense, commerce, treasury,

00:58:48.380 --> 00:58:52.450
attorney general or if
you're an American league fan

00:58:52.450 --> 00:58:53.960
you could create a designated hitter,

00:58:53.960 --> 00:58:57.640
you could have a special
office the Vice Vice President,

00:58:57.640 --> 00:59:00.970
the third in line, in
the line of succession,

00:59:00.970 --> 00:59:02.880
but out of the line of fire

00:59:02.880 --> 00:59:05.960
today, if you were creating
that for the Democrats,

00:59:05.960 --> 00:59:08.400
it would probably be Barack Obama.

00:59:08.400 --> 00:59:11.010
And for the Republicans, it'd
probably be George W. Bush

00:59:11.010 --> 00:59:14.250
because let me tell you, as
someone who's getting close to,

00:59:14.250 --> 00:59:16.500
I'm seeing the end of life myself

00:59:16.500 --> 00:59:19.280
and worrying about my retirement
plans and all the rest

00:59:19.280 --> 00:59:22.760
something simultaneously to
President, the Vice President

00:59:22.760 --> 00:59:26.350
the markets go down 40% around the world.

00:59:26.350 --> 00:59:28.190
And by the way, other bad things happen

00:59:28.190 --> 00:59:30.560
when markets go down 40% around the world,

00:59:30.560 --> 00:59:32.200
all sorts of hell breaks loose,

00:59:32.200 --> 00:59:35.000
and one person I'd want in that situation

00:59:35.000 --> 00:59:36.550
is someone who knows how to do the job

00:59:36.550 --> 00:59:38.640
'cause they've already done the job,

00:59:38.640 --> 00:59:41.100
who has all the world
leaders on speed dial

00:59:41.100 --> 00:59:43.050
and who knows the protocols and procedures

00:59:43.050 --> 00:59:43.883
and even the codes.

00:59:43.883 --> 00:59:46.940
And that would be Obama
for the Dems and W,

00:59:46.940 --> 00:59:49.030
not Trump when he's soon to be ex,

00:59:49.030 --> 00:59:50.760
but W for the Republicans.

00:59:50.760 --> 00:59:53.250
So but that would be
creating a special office

00:59:53.250 --> 00:59:55.333
designated as the Vice Vice President.

00:59:56.450 --> 00:59:57.690
- If I could just add to that.

00:59:57.690 --> 00:59:59.250
- [Alan] Of course.

00:59:59.250 --> 01:00:03.440
- If you have a vacancy
in the Vice Presidency,

01:00:03.440 --> 01:00:06.840
the inability provisions aren't workable

01:00:06.840 --> 01:00:08.960
requires a Vice President

01:00:08.960 --> 01:00:10.730
- If everything pivots
on the Vice President

01:00:10.730 --> 01:00:12.480
and if it's that's empty

01:00:12.480 --> 01:00:14.620
I think you could interpolate
that's the next in line

01:00:14.620 --> 01:00:17.500
who can kind of act in local, VP,

01:00:17.500 --> 01:00:20.750
but that's an interpolation.

01:00:20.750 --> 01:00:22.250
- Yeah and a lot of proposals

01:00:22.250 --> 01:00:25.500
that came from presidential
succession clinic,

01:00:25.500 --> 01:00:28.823
I think at both Yale, as
well as Fordham Law School.

01:00:30.480 --> 01:00:33.060
- Question for Professor Mayhew

01:00:33.060 --> 01:00:34.880
and again this is a very big question,

01:00:34.880 --> 01:00:38.270
but briefly what are the
historical precedents

01:00:38.270 --> 01:00:40.863
for the national crisis we are seeing now?

01:00:44.750 --> 01:00:45.583
(clears throat)

01:00:45.583 --> 01:00:46.860
- Well, that's a tough one.

01:00:48.500 --> 01:00:50.510
Something like Watergate in some ways

01:00:50.510 --> 01:00:52.720
that is a bad stuff
going on in the Capitol

01:00:52.720 --> 01:00:55.950
induced by the President
which everybody's eased of,

01:00:55.950 --> 01:00:58.713
as everybody sees the
bad stuff that's one.

01:01:00.830 --> 01:01:03.390
That's firstly comes to mind.

01:01:03.390 --> 01:01:05.050
I mean, if you take it just in the terms

01:01:05.050 --> 01:01:09.887
of attacking the Capitol or
the Capitol would be in danger

01:01:09.887 --> 01:01:13.690
is the War of 1812 also
during the Civil War in 1861,

01:01:13.690 --> 01:01:16.860
they Capitol was in
great danger for awhile.

01:01:16.860 --> 01:01:19.330
But Lincoln took over the Presidency.

01:01:19.330 --> 01:01:21.767
It's a matter of luck that they could try

01:01:21.767 --> 01:01:23.713
and just couldn't commit insurrection.

01:01:25.370 --> 01:01:29.183
Those come immediately to mind.

01:01:30.400 --> 01:01:33.430
- David, I would add that
Andrew Johnson is impeached

01:01:33.430 --> 01:01:38.430
for his wild rhetorical
attacks on Congress itself,

01:01:40.130 --> 01:01:43.420
swing around the circle in
1866 and all sorts of things.

01:01:43.420 --> 01:01:45.480
Congress, which has the
power of impeachment

01:01:45.480 --> 01:01:48.130
tends not to like it when
Presidents go a little too far

01:01:48.130 --> 01:01:51.293
in attacking Congress
itself just it seems to me.

01:01:52.600 --> 01:01:54.310
- Good, thank you very much.

01:01:54.310 --> 01:01:56.690
Okay, here's a technical question

01:01:56.690 --> 01:01:59.490
about a majority of the cabinet

01:01:59.490 --> 01:02:02.750
assuming Congress doesn't
designate a different body.

01:02:02.750 --> 01:02:05.800
Does that include, how do you count votes?

01:02:05.800 --> 01:02:08.353
Like what's the denominator in that?

01:02:09.850 --> 01:02:11.180
Basically what's the denominator

01:02:11.180 --> 01:02:12.960
and what's the numerator

01:02:12.960 --> 01:02:14.990
to determine a majority of the cabinet?

01:02:14.990 --> 01:02:19.590
Do we know in the legislative history

01:02:19.590 --> 01:02:22.130
or is there some
constitutional understanding

01:02:22.130 --> 01:02:23.750
about that question?

01:02:23.750 --> 01:02:26.360
- John Feerick says that the
numerator and denominator

01:02:26.360 --> 01:02:28.520
includes acting cabinet officers.

01:02:28.520 --> 01:02:29.850
He says that in the book,

01:02:29.850 --> 01:02:31.630
it says that in a legislative history

01:02:31.630 --> 01:02:34.520
and a certain report at page three

01:02:34.520 --> 01:02:36.530
that I could cite to you.

01:02:36.530 --> 01:02:39.200
And he says that in his most recent op-ed

01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:40.610
in the New York Daily News.

01:02:40.610 --> 01:02:43.010
And so I hope he doesn't
contradict me on this--

01:02:43.900 --> 01:02:46.570
- No, it's, you'll also find that in

01:02:46.570 --> 01:02:50.820
a committee report as
well dealing with the,

01:02:50.820 --> 01:02:53.130
moving down the line in terms of the next

01:02:53.130 --> 01:02:55.811
whoever has charged the powers and duties

01:02:55.811 --> 01:02:58.180
in department if they, like the last week

01:02:58.180 --> 01:03:00.740
we had some secretaries who resigned

01:03:00.740 --> 01:03:03.050
but there are acting secretaries

01:03:03.050 --> 01:03:05.510
who would have the voting power.

01:03:05.510 --> 01:03:07.260
Even if they weren't confirmed,

01:03:07.260 --> 01:03:09.670
which is unfortunate that
they would not be confirmed,

01:03:09.670 --> 01:03:12.680
but that in terms of the disability,

01:03:12.680 --> 01:03:15.350
unlike the succession statute

01:03:15.350 --> 01:03:18.010
that requires a cabinet to have been

01:03:18.900 --> 01:03:21.000
confirmed by Congress.

01:03:21.000 --> 01:03:24.060
Otherwise you don't qualify
in the line of succession.

01:03:24.060 --> 01:03:26.500
- Thank you, there are some questions

01:03:26.500 --> 01:03:29.880
about the 14th Amendment

01:03:31.641 --> 01:03:35.260
and I guess that's
insurrection and rebellion

01:03:36.240 --> 01:03:39.240
the section three provisions

01:03:39.240 --> 01:03:41.750
as I guess an alternative foundation

01:03:43.745 --> 01:03:48.390
for considering removal
of the current President.

01:03:48.390 --> 01:03:50.380
What's your sense of that?

01:03:50.380 --> 01:03:53.753
Either in general or in
particular and both, I guess.

01:03:56.120 --> 01:03:57.950
- A lot of actually people in Congress

01:03:57.950 --> 01:03:59.330
have reached out to me about that.

01:03:59.330 --> 01:04:00.490
I've been in conversation

01:04:00.490 --> 01:04:02.650
with 10 different scholars about that.

01:04:02.650 --> 01:04:06.260
Truthfully don't pay attention
to a bunch of op-eds on this.

01:04:06.260 --> 01:04:07.910
There's a lot of sloppy thinking on that.

01:04:07.910 --> 01:04:10.970
Let's just not focus on
that right now, truthfully.

01:04:10.970 --> 01:04:13.920
I think it's mistaken in variety of ways

01:04:13.920 --> 01:04:17.563
that it won't hold up
under long-term analysis.

01:04:19.643 --> 01:04:22.540
- Other thoughts on that?

01:04:22.540 --> 01:04:26.240
Okay, no, let's see.

01:04:26.240 --> 01:04:31.240
Okay, sorry, moving up the list.

01:04:32.550 --> 01:04:37.550
Okay, given where we
are on January 11, 2021,

01:04:37.730 --> 01:04:42.100
do you think that invoking
the 25th Amendment now

01:04:42.100 --> 01:04:44.870
would have some important impacts?

01:04:44.870 --> 01:04:47.050
You mentioned, for example that

01:04:47.050 --> 01:04:50.480
Donald J. Trump could
no longer give pardons,

01:04:50.480 --> 01:04:52.160
what other reasons might there be

01:04:52.160 --> 01:04:55.350
why this might be
something important to do

01:04:55.350 --> 01:04:57.280
or if you think it's important

01:04:57.280 --> 01:04:58.230
what are some of the reasons

01:04:58.230 --> 01:04:59.980
why you might think it's important to do?

01:04:59.980 --> 01:05:04.980
- Now I store a reference and students

01:05:06.160 --> 01:05:09.000
making reference to the
use of presidential power

01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:11.860
in terms of using our military might

01:05:11.860 --> 01:05:14.670
and that might affect relationships

01:05:14.670 --> 01:05:17.120
with countries in other
parts of the world.

01:05:17.120 --> 01:05:20.440
That the new President
will have to deal with.

01:05:20.440 --> 01:05:25.440
If it was an exercise of power

01:05:25.490 --> 01:05:30.090
in areas like that could
raise questions about

01:05:31.060 --> 01:05:33.840
whether it was an
appropriate use of the power

01:05:33.840 --> 01:05:35.540
because of what's going on right now,

01:05:35.540 --> 01:05:37.540
which might be a reason that some say

01:05:38.630 --> 01:05:40.763
calls for the use of the 25th Amendment.

01:05:41.640 --> 01:05:43.720
- To the full powers of the President

01:05:43.720 --> 01:05:46.760
under the 25th Amendment
are being relocated

01:05:46.760 --> 01:05:48.350
to the Vice President.

01:05:48.350 --> 01:05:51.780
So that's so, and I won't
speak about this President

01:05:51.780 --> 01:05:54.805
but if you imagine that you
actually had a President

01:05:54.805 --> 01:05:57.170
of whom there was a real
question of mental confidence.

01:05:57.170 --> 01:05:59.240
You want that person's
finger on the button.

01:05:59.240 --> 01:06:02.570
That's what Americans were focusing on

01:06:02.570 --> 01:06:04.810
in the wake of Hiroshima and Nagasaki

01:06:04.810 --> 01:06:07.610
when Jack Kennedy is killed.

01:06:07.610 --> 01:06:11.420
And in a way we're lucky,
truthfully, this is very hard.

01:06:11.420 --> 01:06:14.170
I hate even saying it
myself, but we were lucky

01:06:14.170 --> 01:06:16.640
that he was killed and not merely deranged

01:06:16.640 --> 01:06:19.320
because if he was deranged
in a nuclear world

01:06:19.320 --> 01:06:22.810
and he doesn't recognize
his own mental inability

01:06:22.810 --> 01:06:23.917
so there has to be a mechanism

01:06:23.917 --> 01:06:26.150
and the 25th Amendment provides one

01:06:26.150 --> 01:06:28.550
for someone competent to come in

01:06:28.550 --> 01:06:30.980
if he's not all there in a nuclear world.

01:06:30.980 --> 01:06:33.800
And that's partly what John meant

01:06:33.800 --> 01:06:36.400
when he talked about the military.

01:06:36.400 --> 01:06:39.990
Now it's not just that Mike
Pence and that the President

01:06:39.990 --> 01:06:42.240
would lose the power to give pardons

01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:45.420
if he handed over power
voluntarily under section three

01:06:45.420 --> 01:06:49.020
or was relieved of command
under section four,

01:06:49.020 --> 01:06:51.260
think of the Kane Mutineer
or something like that

01:06:51.260 --> 01:06:53.660
when the captain is relieved of command.

01:06:53.660 --> 01:06:55.070
Okay, so he can't give pardons anymore

01:06:55.070 --> 01:06:57.530
but here's a little interesting
wrinkle truth be told.

01:06:57.530 --> 01:07:00.310
If I'm trying to sweet talk
Trump into taking this thing,

01:07:00.310 --> 01:07:01.830
'cause I wish he would step down

01:07:01.830 --> 01:07:04.140
'cause I'll be able to sleep
better for the next week.

01:07:04.140 --> 01:07:08.650
Ooh, when you stepped down
you can't give pardons anymore

01:07:08.650 --> 01:07:10.510
but you could never have
pardoned yourself anyway,

01:07:10.510 --> 01:07:11.500
that would have been improper.

01:07:11.500 --> 01:07:12.940
Well, but you can get a pardon now

01:07:12.940 --> 01:07:14.810
because someone else's President.

01:07:14.810 --> 01:07:17.873
So you at least have the
possibility of that now don't you?

01:07:19.780 --> 01:07:21.710
And if there were a deal a prearrangement

01:07:21.710 --> 01:07:23.870
that would itself be impeachable,

01:07:23.870 --> 01:07:27.860
perhaps but you remember Ford
pardoned Nixon in theory,

01:07:27.860 --> 01:07:30.380
if the 25th Amendment were activated

01:07:30.380 --> 01:07:32.900
Pence would be making pardon decisions

01:07:32.900 --> 01:07:35.560
for all sorts of people,
including the Trumps.

01:07:35.560 --> 01:07:36.820
I'm just saying

01:07:38.240 --> 01:07:41.400
- Okay, David, do you
have anything you'd like

01:07:41.400 --> 01:07:43.163
to add to this?

01:07:44.740 --> 01:07:47.203
Okay, good, are there future,

01:07:50.830 --> 01:07:53.700
are there actions future
presidential administrations

01:07:53.700 --> 01:07:56.340
can or should take to ameliorate the gaps

01:07:56.340 --> 01:07:59.880
or ambiguities we currently
see in the succession process

01:07:59.880 --> 01:08:02.900
short of supporting
constitutional amendments?

01:08:02.900 --> 01:08:05.330
So are there a couple of key things

01:08:05.330 --> 01:08:10.330
that we might wanna do I guess
from a statutory standpoint?

01:08:10.550 --> 01:08:13.210
- Yeah, the Succession Act is dangerous.

01:08:13.210 --> 01:08:15.010
It's an accident waiting to happen.

01:08:15.010 --> 01:08:18.630
Anyone who for example, was a fan

01:08:18.630 --> 01:08:22.210
of the West Wing TV series,
it makes no sense at all.

01:08:22.210 --> 01:08:24.910
There was a vacant Vice Presidency.

01:08:24.910 --> 01:08:27.380
So Martin Sheen had to
step aside temporarily.

01:08:27.380 --> 01:08:31.680
And you have voted for a liberal
Democrat from New England,

01:08:31.680 --> 01:08:33.120
and you ended up with John Goodman

01:08:33.120 --> 01:08:36.540
who's this conservative
Republican, that makes no sense.

01:08:36.540 --> 01:08:40.400
And then Jed Bartlett,
spoiler alert comes back

01:08:40.400 --> 01:08:42.150
to the Presidency eight days later.

01:08:42.150 --> 01:08:43.470
And meanwhile, John Goodman's

01:08:43.470 --> 01:08:45.610
had to give up this Speakership,

01:08:45.610 --> 01:08:48.750
and the seat in the House of
Representatives for eight days.

01:08:48.750 --> 01:08:50.560
it's a completely bonkers system

01:08:50.560 --> 01:08:53.160
and we gotta change it
before someone gets hurt.

01:08:53.160 --> 01:08:56.250
And that requires a
statute, a new statute.

01:08:56.250 --> 01:08:58.500
And the Continuity of
Government Commission

01:08:58.500 --> 01:09:01.620
agrees with me about all
this, this is post 9/11,

01:09:01.620 --> 01:09:03.776
and had a lot of
distinguished people on it,

01:09:03.776 --> 01:09:07.350
there was Brookings on one
side and AEI on the other

01:09:07.350 --> 01:09:10.930
included past Speakers of the
House including Newt Gingrich

01:09:10.930 --> 01:09:14.010
and they agree with me
that this is a really

01:09:14.010 --> 01:09:17.090
a dangerous statute that
needs to be modified.

01:09:17.090 --> 01:09:19.110
- Thank you.
- I would add three things

01:09:20.530 --> 01:09:24.050
further clarification on the
issue of acting secretaries.

01:09:24.050 --> 01:09:28.130
I think that that should be
expressed a little bit more

01:09:28.130 --> 01:09:31.523
in the presidential
succession statute area.

01:09:32.440 --> 01:09:37.440
Number two, Professor
Amar, I think focused on

01:09:37.470 --> 01:09:39.480
whether you wanna have
the legislative leaders

01:09:39.480 --> 01:09:41.840
and a possible interruption

01:09:41.840 --> 01:09:44.370
if you're changing parties and midstream

01:09:45.300 --> 01:09:48.760
and that might call for a
different line of succession

01:09:48.760 --> 01:09:50.840
perhaps a cabinet line of succession,

01:09:50.840 --> 01:09:53.830
similar to what we had in 1886.

01:09:53.830 --> 01:09:56.490
And a raft of proposals to
deal with issues such as

01:09:56.490 --> 01:09:58.698
a dual disability at the same time

01:09:58.698 --> 01:10:01.050
with the President and
Vice President to make it,

01:10:01.050 --> 01:10:03.573
to clarify who judges that.

01:10:05.060 --> 01:10:07.860
- Good, a quick question.

01:10:07.860 --> 01:10:11.140
Does the President have
the power to self pardon?

01:10:11.140 --> 01:10:12.790
Do we think the President can self pardon?

01:10:12.790 --> 01:10:14.930
Is that a thing?

01:10:14.930 --> 01:10:17.780
- It's a first principle,
the constitution is law,

01:10:17.780 --> 01:10:20.160
law presupposes the rule of law

01:10:20.160 --> 01:10:23.850
and the rule of law for 2000
years going back to the Romans

01:10:23.850 --> 01:10:27.670
and through Blackstone is
that no one can be a judge

01:10:27.670 --> 01:10:31.360
in his own case, nemo iudex in causa sua

01:10:31.360 --> 01:10:35.290
the deep, deep fundamental
principle of law and justice.

01:10:35.290 --> 01:10:38.350
So I think that the very
concept of pardoning yourself

01:10:38.350 --> 01:10:39.440
is a sham.

01:10:39.440 --> 01:10:40.380
- Okay, thank you.

01:10:40.380 --> 01:10:43.750
So I have a final question,
just to wrap up question.

01:10:43.750 --> 01:10:46.880
I like to ask in these
panels, first of all,

01:10:46.880 --> 01:10:49.380
if there's any last comments

01:10:49.380 --> 01:10:51.570
that any panelists would like to make

01:10:51.570 --> 01:10:53.110
and we'll go in turn.

01:10:53.110 --> 01:10:56.050
And then also, is there anything
that you would recommend

01:10:56.050 --> 01:11:00.980
to our audience that you would
recommend that they read?

01:11:00.980 --> 01:11:05.210
A book or articles either to understand

01:11:05.210 --> 01:11:06.980
the 25th Amendment better

01:11:06.980 --> 01:11:09.150
or that you've found personally

01:11:09.150 --> 01:11:11.560
especially illuminating regarding

01:11:11.560 --> 01:11:14.450
the current political situation

01:11:14.450 --> 01:11:16.080
without going into what I consider to be

01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:17.700
the current political situation.

01:11:17.700 --> 01:11:19.120
I'll let you interpret that

01:11:19.120 --> 01:11:20.960
but anything that you've read recently

01:11:20.960 --> 01:11:23.370
or anything that you
would recommend reading

01:11:23.370 --> 01:11:27.130
that you found especially
enlightening and illuminating.

01:11:27.130 --> 01:11:29.780
And could we go maybe in reverse order,

01:11:29.780 --> 01:11:31.693
David, John, and then Akhil.

01:11:32.640 --> 01:11:34.730
- I'll pass to John and Akhil

01:11:34.730 --> 01:11:39.730
- Okay, David has passed.

01:11:39.920 --> 01:11:44.733
- Oh, thank you, I would say three things.

01:11:46.240 --> 01:11:48.820
First book that I reached
when I had a question

01:11:48.820 --> 01:11:51.290
about section four, the 14th Amendment

01:11:51.290 --> 01:11:53.697
was Professor Amar's book

01:11:53.697 --> 01:11:55.740
"A Biography of The Constitution."

01:11:55.740 --> 01:11:59.760
I consider it a classic
and it gives gets me

01:11:59.760 --> 01:12:03.030
into appreciating the constitution

01:12:03.030 --> 01:12:04.853
when I start into that book.

01:12:06.070 --> 01:12:10.500
The second thing that took me time to do

01:12:10.500 --> 01:12:14.840
was a very short article
